# Native projects are generated by `expo prebuild` (CNG) from app.json, so they
# are build output, not source. Committing them means every config change has
# two places to go wrong. Regenerate with: pnpm exec expo prebuild --clean
/android
/ios

# NOT ignored, deliberately: google-services.json.
#
# It looks like a credential and isn't one. It carries the FCM sender id and an
# API key that ships inside every copy of the APK, so anyone with the app already
# has it; Google's own guidance is that it is safe in version control, and the key
# is restricted by package name and signing certificate rather than by secrecy.
#
# It also cannot be ignored in practice: EAS builds from the archive it uploads,
# which respects this file, and the Google Services Gradle plugin fails the build
# outright when the file is absent. Ignoring it breaks every cloud build.
#
# The real secret is the FCM V1 service-account key, which lives in EAS and never
# touches the repo.

